ith Vietnamese translations","Terms with Welsh translations","Terms with West Frisian translations","en:Lakes","en:Places in Austria","en:Places in Germany","en:Places in Switzerland"],"links":[["lake","lake"],["Rhine","Rhine"],["Germany","Germany#English"],["Bavaria","Bavaria"],["Baden-Württemberg","Baden-Württemberg"],["Switzerland","Switzerland#English"],["St. Gallen","St. Gallen"],["Thurgau","Thurgau"],["Schaffhausen","Schaffhausen"],["Austria","Austria#English"],["Vorarlberg","Vorarlberg"],["Obersee","Obersee"],["Überlinger See","Überlinger See"],["Untersee","Untersee"]],"glosses":["A lake on the Rhine located at the intersection of Germany (Bavaria and Baden-Württemberg), Switzerland (St. Gallen, Thurgau and Schaffhausen) and Austria (Vorarlberg). It consists of two parts, the Obersee in the east and northwest (Überlinger See) and the much smaller Untersee in the west."],"id":"9073de20-56d1-454d-bda7-e2828973bbec"}],"related":[{"word":"Konstanz"},{"word":"Friedrichshafen"},{"word":"Radolfzell am Bodensee"},{"word":"Bregenz"},{"word":"Lindau"},{"word":"Reichenau"},{"word":"Mainau"}],"synonyms":[]},"lake michigan-huron":{"id":"060ea6f6-e616-4d85-b1df-1bfeab36e8d1","word":"Lake Michigan-Huron","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"one of the Great Lakes","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Lago Michigan-Huron"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"As backwater from Lake Erie raises the level of Lake St. Clair, so backwater from Lake St. Clair raises the level of Lake Michigan-Huron.","ref":"1910, US Congress, Report of the International Waterways Commission on the Regulation of Lake Erie, page 10:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[117,136]],"id":"9785c6af-b21f-4707-b7e0-7e8a06e10418"},{"text":"The inflow to Lake Michigan–Huron, through the St. Marys River, from Lake Superior was determined each day... Similarly, the outflow from Lake Michigan–Huron to Lake Erie was determined for each day...","ref":"1922, John Hayford, Effects of Winds and of Barometric Pressures on the Great Lakes, Carnegie Institution of Washington, page 28:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[14,33],[138,157]],"id":"b5f97cb5-4c71-49f6-85ba-8e01bff40000"},{"text":"Contrary to popular belief, the largest lake in the world is not Lake Superior but mighty Lake Michigan-Huron, which is a single hydrological unit linked at the Straits of Mackinac. Of all the Great Lakes, Michigan-Huron is the least regulated...","ref":"2004, Canadian geographic, volume 124, Royal Canadian Geographical Society, page 96:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[90,109]],"id":"2a9201ae-6e8f-490e-931d-e7810520b771"},{"text":"Of the Great Lakes, Lake Michigan-Huron had the highest water levels in midsummer and Lake Superior, in early fall.","ref":"2006, Magnuson, Kratz, & Benson, Long-term dynamics of lakes in the landscape, page 132:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[20,39]],"id":"29cc2063-d3dc-4122-92d8-32f0c6f67555"}],"links":[["Great Lakes","Great Lakes"],["Lake Michigan","Lake Michigan"],["Lake Huron","Lake Huron"]],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English proper nouns","English terms with quotations","English uncountable nouns","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Danish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Lao translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Thai translations","en:Lakes"],"glosses":["One of the Great Lakes of North America. Hydrologically a single lake, its two basins are traditionally counted as separate lakes, Lake Michigan and Lake Huron."],"id":"7aa1e9fb-645c-4f4a-b270-91843f1521ae"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"lake victoria":{"id":"2cee08b3-91cd-459c-aa49-9c527aa06c36","word":"Lake Victoria","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Afri